  "body": "Found while #4233 took the merge of #4249 (#3646).\n\nWhat happens: a document component row can hold `milling` (the catalog facts of a multi-seat cutter body) and `running` (the tool material and the cutting rows of an insert). The project file (v84) and `.camtools` v8 save the two keys. The user component library (`camcraft-components/1`) does not hold them:\n- A library file with the keys is refused by name.\n- `LibraryComponent::from_row` refuses a document row with the keys by name. A save to the library of such a row is refused (MCP `save_library_component`, the UI \"save to My library\").\n- A sync keeps the facts and the data of the document row. The content hash does not include them.\n\nExpected: a user can keep a multi-seat cutter body or an insert with its facts in the library, and a sync brings them into a document.\n\nWork:\n- Add `milling` and `running` to `LibraryComponent`, to the library file (a version step or optional keys) and to the content hash.\n- A sync copies them from the library copy, through the row law.\n- Change the callers that build a `LibraryComponent` (built-ins, UI, MCP, tests).\n\nDone means: a library round trip of a multi-seat body and of an insert with running data is identical, a sync lands them in the document in one undo step, and the refusals above are removed.\n",
